{"id":"S1131","name":"NPPSPY","description":"NPPSPY is an implementation of a theoretical mechanism first presented in 2004 for capturing credentials submitted to a Windows system via a rogue Network Provider API item. NPPSPY captures credentials following submission and writes them to a file on the victim system for follow-on exfiltration.","kind":"attack_tool","upstream_type":"tool","stix_id":"tool--0630d1a7-54da-4a48-a6af-eb8a62b13c17","source_modified":"2024-10-28T19:00:14.732Z","aliases":["NPPSPY"],"platforms":["Windows"],"source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1131","source_domains":["enterprise"],"classification_note":"Included because the active pinned ATT&CK object has type tool. This is an upstream classification, not an assurance of benignness or a recommendation to run it.","page":"tools/S1131/","reviewed_on":"2026-09-27","guides":[],"guide_currentness":"Historical guides retain publication dates. Commands and product availability have not been revalidated.","techniques":[{"key":"enterprise/T1005","id":"T1005","name":"Data from Local System","domain":"enterprise","page":"techniques/enterprise/T1005/","environments":["cloud-hosted-endpoint","network-infrastructure","onprem","virtualization"],"platforms":["ESXi","Linux","macOS","Network Devices","Windows"],"bases":["attack_uses"],"evidence":[{"basis":"attack_uses","relationship_id":"relationship--69bdad3f-929c-4597-a9d7-4ec2c738170d","description":"NPPSPY records data entered from the local system logon at Winlogon to capture credentials in cleartext.","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1131","source_commit":"6cda5ad8462c79e14fbb872f4e09059b18e0cfc4","citations":[{"title":"Dray Agha. (2022, August 16). Cleartext Shenanigans: Gifting User Passwords to Adversaries With NPPSPY. Retrieved May 17, 2024.","url":"https://www.huntress.com/blog/cleartext-shenanigans-gifting-user-passwords-to-adversaries-with-nppspy"}]}],"telemetry_references":[{"id":"DC0064","name":"Command Execution","tag":"